---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config.mjs';

const updated = '8 September 2026';
const mail = SITE.contactEmail;
---

<Layout
  title={`Privacy Policy — ${SITE.name}`}
  description="What this site collects, why, who else sees it and how to get it deleted. Written to the GDPR, in plain English."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-16">
    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl font-bold text-ink">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="prose prose-sm mt-8 max-w-none text-muted prose-headings:font-serif prose-headings:text-ink prose-strong:text-ink prose-a:text-terracotta">
      <p class="lead">
        This is a small, one-person site that writes about home decor and links to Amazon. It is not
        an advertising business and it has no interest in following you around. Here is exactly what
        happens to your data, in the order it happens.
      </p>

      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name} is run by an independent publisher based in Slovenia, in the European Union. For
        anything on this page, including a request to see or delete your data, write to
        {mail
          ? <a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a>
          : <mark class="rounded bg-terracotta/15 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs text-terracotta-dark">[ contact email ]</mark>}
        and you will get an answer within one month, as the GDPR requires. That mailbox is the
        controller&rsquo;s contact point; no data protection officer is appointed, and none is
        required at this size.
      </p>

      <h2>Reading the site</h2>
      <p>
        You can read every page here without giving anything. There is no account, no login and no
        contact form. Our host, Cloudflare, keeps ordinary server logs (IP address, browser, the
        page requested, the time) to keep the site up and to absorb attacks. That is our legitimate
        interest under Article 6(1)(f) GDPR, and those logs are short-lived.
      </p>
      <p>
        The fonts you are reading are served from this domain, not from Google, so your browser
        never asks Google for them.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics, only if you say yes</h2>
      <p>
        We would like to know which pages get read. That is Google Analytics 4, and it needs
        cookies, so it runs on your consent under Article 6(1)(a) GDPR and nothing else. Until you
        press <em>Accept analytics</em>, the Google script is never downloaded and no request
        reaches Google at all. Google Consent Mode is set to deny advertising storage permanently,
        so your visit is never used to build an advertising profile, and IP anonymisation is on.
      </p>
      <p>
        Google Ireland Limited is the processor, with onward transfer to Google LLC in the United
        States under the EU&ndash;U.S. Data Privacy Framework. Data is kept 14 months and then
        deleted. Everything set, and how to withdraw, is on the
        <a href="/cookies">cookie policy</a> page.
      </p>

      <h2>The newsletter</h2>
      <p>
        If you type your email into the signup box and press subscribe, we store that email so we
        can send you the newsletter. That is consent under Article 6(1)(a) GDPR, given by you
        pressing the button after reading what the box says.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>What we hold:</strong> your email address, the date you subscribed, and whether
          you opened the last few emails.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Who processes it:</strong> Brevo (Sendinblue SAS), a French company, acting as our
          processor under Article 28 GDPR. Their servers are in the European Union, so your email
          address does not leave the EEA for this purpose. See
          <a href="https://www.brevo.com/legal/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">their privacy policy</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>How long:</strong> until you unsubscribe. Every email has a one-click unsubscribe
          link, and using it deletes you from the list. You can also just write to us.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>We never sell or rent the list</strong>, and we do not use it for anything except
          the newsletter itself.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Amazon links</h2>
      <p>
        Every product link here goes to Amazon and carries our affiliate tag. When you click one,
        Amazon may set its own cookies so a purchase can be attributed to us. That happens on
        Amazon&rsquo;s side, under
        <a href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/help/customer/display.html?nodeId=468496" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Amazon&rsquo;s Privacy Notice</a>,
        and we never see who bought what. We receive only anonymous totals: how many items were
        ordered and what commission was earned. No names, no addresses, no order details.
      </p>
      <p>
        Full detail of the commercial relationship is on the
        <a href="/disclosure">affiliate disclosure</a> page.
      </p>

      <h2>Product images</h2>
      <p>
        Product photographs are served from Amazon&rsquo;s own image servers, so your browser
        requests them from Amazon and Amazon sees your IP address for that request. This is how
        Amazon requires their images to be used, and it happens on every page that shows products.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under Chapter III of the GDPR you can ask for a copy of what we hold (Article 15), have it
        corrected (16), have it deleted (17), have its use restricted (18), have it sent to you in a
        machine-readable file (20), object to anything based on legitimate interest (21) and
        withdraw consent at any time (7(3)). One email to the address above starts any of them, and
        it costs nothing. There is no automated decision-making or profiling here within the meaning
        of Article 22.
      </p>

      <h2>If you think we got it wrong</h2>
      <p>
        Tell us first, it is usually fixable the same day. But under Article 77 GDPR you can also
        complain directly to a supervisory authority. In Slovenia that is the
        <a href="https://www.ip-rs.si/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Informacijski pooblaščenec</a>,
        Dunajska cesta 22, 1000 Ljubljana, <a href="mailto:gp.ip@ip-rs.si">gp.ip@ip-rs.si</a>. If you
        live elsewhere in the EU or EEA, your own national authority works too.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site is written for adults furnishing their own homes. We do not knowingly collect data
        from anyone under 16. If you believe a child has subscribed, write to us and it will be
        deleted.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If we add a tool or change a provider, this page changes with it and the date at the top
        moves. Older versions are available on request.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
